{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e0U6NMtqT_mcLlogF",
			"description": "Bolt Pistol, Godwyn-De'az Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The human-portable bolt pistol, most commonly the Godwyn-De'az pattern that shares its mass-reactive .75-calibre round with the standard Godwyn boltgun, is issued to Inquisitorial acolytes, commissars, veteran officers and other elite humans rather than to rank-and-file Guardsmen, who are more usually equipped with an autopistol or laspistol if they carry a sidearm at all. Dark Heresy and Rogue Trader both depict it as a prized, LC1 weapon whose recoil is punishing for an unaugmented shooter.\n\nDesign: Scaled down one die from the Godwyn boltgun anchor (6d(2) pi+, see the standard Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern entry) to 5d(2) pi+: the bolt's rocket motor ignites a few metres clear of the muzzle and does most of the accelerating, so a shorter pistol barrel costs less damage than a conventional gunpowder round would lose, but it still loses something to the reduced initial propellant charge and shorter sighting radius. The follow-up scales the same way from the boltgun's 3d cr ex anchor. ST 10† and Rcl 3 are both unusually high for a service pistol (compare a normal GURPS pistol's ST 8-9, Rcl 2): this is the \"hard for unaugmented humans to handle\" property the fiction keeps returning to. The † lets it be fired two-handed at the listed ST; fired one-handed by anyone under ST 10 it takes the standard extra recoil and reduced accuracy for shooting under minimum ST. Special ammunition (Kraken, Hellfire, etc.) is not repeated here; see the Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern entry for full stats, all of which are loaded in .75-calibre pistol form as well as rifle form per Deathwatch's Special Issue Ammunition rules.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "500",
