		{
			"id": "ekSS6Rcz6z5S5nL-l",
			"description": "Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Godwyn-De'az pattern is the boltgun the fiction treats as the baseline: a self-contained, rocket-assisted .75-calibre round whose motor ignites a few metres clear of the muzzle, widely depicted (Horus Heresy and modern Black Library alike) as capable of blowing an unarmoured man apart and reliably punching through carapace plate, while a Space Marine can shrug off a few hits from another Marine's boltgun before going down. Special Issue Ammunition (Kraken, Hellfire, Metal Storm, Vengeance) is Deathwatch's own term and rulebook material; Inferno bolts are that line's Deathwatch-specific incendiary load; sanctified/blessed ammunition is a recurring detail in Adepta Sororitas and Chaplain background with no stated mechanical difference against armour.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed boltgun anchor: 6d(2) pi+ with a 3d cr ex follow-up (per the framework's damage table). Against a torso DR 40 suit of Astartes power armour the armour divisor (2) drops effective DR to 20; 6d(2) averages 21, so it usually needs several hits to punch through and then still has to beat the wearer's HP with the wounding bonus, matching \"a Marine takes several bolts to kill another Marine.\" Against carapace (DR 20, effective DR 10) it penetrates easily, and against an unarmoured man it is instantly lethal, both as the framework specifies. Kraken swaps the armour divisor to (3) and drops the wounding modifier from pi+ to pi (less internal fragmentation, more punch) - effective DR 40/3 ≈ 13, and the dice are unchanged, so its edge over a standard round is entirely in the armour divisor. Hellfire and Metal Storm are built from Deathwatch's stated design intent (anti-organic, anti-horde) translated into GURPS damage types (tox for the bio-payload, a fragmentation bracket for the flechette cloud) rather than lifted from any catalogue entry. Vengeance and sanctified rounds are modelled as unchanged ballistically, since neither RPG nor Codex material describes a different penetrator, with their special property left as a notes-level rule the GM applies.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1200",
